From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: program the farrow resampler at 2.4 GHz 40 MHz

The farrow resampler was left unprogrammed on 2.4 GHz at 40 MHz, with
whatever the previous channel left in 0x0199-0x01a3 and the per-core
deltaphase. wl 7.14 programs it with the 2.4 GHz mode at the bonded
centre frequency: on the RT-AC66U B1 at ch6/40 (2447 MHz) the ratio
0x16f0ccd and deltaphase 0x594621 of the same formula.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -11156,16 +11156,13 @@ static void b43_phy_ac_farrow_setup(stru
 			   B43_PHY_AC_STATE_RX_CCK | B43_PHY_AC_STATE_RX_OFDM |
 			   B43_PHY_AC_STATE_CCA_RESET);
 
-	if (b43_current_band(dev->wl) == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ) {
-		if (width != NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20) {
-			b43_phy_ac_todo(dev,
-				"Farrow resampler not programmed at "
-				"2.4 GHz with width %d: not measured\n",
-				width);
-			return;
-		}
+	/*
+	 * 2.4 GHz uses its own mode at 20 and 40 MHz: wl 7.14 on the
+	 * RT-AC66U B1 at ch6/40 (centre 2447 MHz) writes the ratio and
+	 * deltaphase of this formula, 0x16f0ccd and 0x594621.
+	 */
+	if (b43_current_band(dev->wl) == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)
 		m = &b43_phy_ac_farrow_mode_2g_20;
-	}
 
 	/*
 	 * The operating channel's centre frequency, and the mode that goes
